/-!
# The generic-rank decomposition of flatness in dimensions at least the fibre dimension

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a smooth morphism with geometrically irreducible fibres of dimension `d`
and let `F` be an `𝒪_X`-module of finite presentation. Then `F` is flat over `S` in dimensions
`≥ d` exactly when, for every fibre, `F` is free of some finite rank on a neighbourhood of that
fibre's generic point.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_freeAtPointOfRank_of_isFlatOverInDimensionsGE`: flatness in
  dimensions `≥ d` forces freeness of some rank near the generic point of every fibre.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOverAt_of_freeAtPointOfRank`: a module free of finite rank near a
  point of the source of a smooth morphism is flat over the base there.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_of_forall_exists_freeAtPointOfRank`: the
  converse, which holds because a smooth morphism is flat.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_iff_forall_exists_freeAtPointOfRank`:
  **Stacks 05UE**, the two taken together.

## Implementation notes

The condition `𝒪_X`-free of rank `p` near the generic point of every fibre is the functor `H_p`
of Stacks 05MP, formalized as `AlgebraicGeometry.FreeAtPointOfRank` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FreeAtGenericPointsSituation.Condition`, and flatness in dimensions `≥ d` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverInDimensionsGE` of Stacks 0CWG, the condition whose functor is the
`F_d` of the source. The equivalence below is therefore the equality of `F_d` with the union of
the subfunctors `H_p`: all the hypotheses are stable under base change, so the statement over
`S` already carries the statement over every scheme `T` over `S`.

The forward direction is the argument of the source. The non-flat locus in a fibre is closed by
Stacks 05M9, so if it contained the generic point it would be the whole fibre and have
dimension `d` rather than less; hence `F` is flat over `S` at that generic point. The fibre is
smooth over the residue field and geometrically irreducible, so it is integral and its local
ring at the generic point is the function field, over which every module is free; Stacks 080Q
then produces the free neighbourhood.

The converse needs that a smooth morphism is flat: freeness of finite rank near a point makes
the module finite locally free on a neighbourhood, hence flat over the base there, so the
generic point lies outside the non-flat locus, which is then a proper closed subset of an
irreducible fibre of dimension `d` and so has dimension less than `d`.

The hypotheses `F.IsQuasicoherent` and `F.IsFiniteType` are carried alongside
`F.IsFinitePresentation` because they are what `AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverInDimensionsGE`
requires for its statement to be well formed and instance search does not produce them from
finite presentation.

## What is not proved

The source states the decomposition as `F_d = ∐_{p = 0, …, c} H_p`, an equality of functors on
schemes over `S`. Two further ingredients of that packaging are not established here.

* The bound `c`: that `F` is generated by `c` global sections on the affine `X`, hence that
  `H_p` is empty for `p > c`, so that the union is finite.
* That the union is a *coproduct* of Zariski sheaves, which also needs the rank to be locally
  constant on the base and the functor `F_d` itself, i.e. the functor attached to Situation
  Stacks 05MT by (Stacks 05MU); the library carries the condition `IsFlatOverInDimensionsGE`
  but not that functor.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05UE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05UE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05MP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05MP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CWG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CWG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05M9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05M9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080Q)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The fibre of a smooth morphism over a point with geometrically irreducible fibre is an
irreducible space. -/
private theorem irreducibleSpace_fiber_of_geometricallyIrreducible {X S : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X ⟶ S) [Smooth f] (s : S)
    (hgs : GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s)) :
    IrreducibleSpace (f.fiber s) :=
  GeometricallyIrreducible.irreducibleSpace (f := f.fiberToSpecResidueField s)
    (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s).isOpenMap

/-- For a smooth family with geometrically irreducible fibres, the restriction of any module to
a fibre has flat stalk at the fibre's generic point: the fibre is smooth over a field and
irreducible, hence integral, so its local ring there is the function field. -/
private theorem flat_fiber_stalk_isGenericPoint {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) [Smooth f]
    (x : X) (hξ : IsGenericPoint (f.asFiber x) (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber (f x))))
    (hgeom : GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField (f x))) (F : X.Modules) :
    letI := Stacks.Flatness.stalkModule
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (f.fiberι (f x))).obj F) (f.asFiber x)
    Module.Flat (ToType ((f.fiber (f x)).presheaf.stalk (f.asFiber x)))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u})
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (f.fiberι (f x))).obj F).val.presheaf (f.asFiber x))) := by
  let Y := f.fiber (f x)
  let g := f.fiberToSpecResidueField (f x)
  let G := (Scheme.Modules.pullback (f.fiberι (f x))).obj F
  let y := f.asFiber x
  have : IrreducibleSpace Y := irreducibleSpace_fiber_of_geometricallyIrreducible f (f x) hgeom
  have hSmooth : Smooth g := by
    show Smooth (pullback.snd f (S.fromSpecResidueField (f x)))
    exact MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange.of_isPullback
      (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (S.fromSpecResidueField (f x))) ‹Smooth f›
  have : IsReduced Y :=
    (geometricallyReduced_of_smooth g).geometrically_isReduced
      (y := 𝟙 (Spec (.of (S.residueField (f x))))) (fst := 𝟙 Y) (snd := g) IsPullback.of_id_fst
  let A := ToType (Y.presheaf.stalk y)
  let M := ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) G.val.presheaf y)
  let _ : Module A M := Stacks.Flatness.stalkModule G y
  let _ : Field A := (isField_stalk_of_isGenericPoint y hξ).toField
  have : Module.Free A M := Module.Free.of_divisionRing A M
  exact Module.Flat.of_free

/-- A closed subset of an irreducible space of dimension `d` missing a generic point has
dimension less than `d`: a chain of irreducible closed subsets of it extends by the whole
space. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_lt_of_isClosed_notMem {T : Type*} [TopologicalSpace T]
    [IrreducibleSpace T] {C : Set T} (hC : IsClosed C) (ξ : T) (hξC : ξ ∉ C) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : topologicalKrullDim T = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    topologicalKrullDim (↥C) < (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  rw [topologicalKrullDim, Order.krullDim_lt_coe_iff]
  intro p
  have hinc : Topology.IsInducing (Subtype.val : C → T) := Topology.IsInducing.subtypeVal
  have hmono : StrictMono (IrreducibleCloseds.map (Subtype.val : C → T) hinc.continuous) :=
    IrreducibleCloseds.map_strictMono_of_isInducing hinc
  let q := p.map (IrreducibleCloseds.map (Subtype.val : C → T) hinc.continuous) hmono
  have hsub : (q.last : Set T) ⊆ C := by
    show closure (Subtype.val '' (p.last : Set C)) ⊆ C
    exact closure_minimal (Set.image_subset_iff.mpr fun z _ ↦ z.2) hC
  let whole : IrreducibleCloseds T := ⟨Set.univ, IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ T,
    isClosed_univ⟩
  have hlast : q.last < whole := by
    refine lt_of_le_of_ne (Set.subset_univ _) fun heq ↦ ?_
    exact hξC (hsub (by simp [heq, whole]))
  have hq : ((q.snoc whole hlast).length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ topologicalKrullDim T := by
    simpa [topologicalKrullDim] using Order.LTSeries.length_le_krullDim (q.snoc whole hlast)
  rw [hd] at hq
  have hqNat : ((q.snoc whole hlast).length : ℕ) ≤ d :=
    ENat.natCast_le_natCast.mp (WithBot.coe_le_coe.mp hq)
  have hlen : (q.snoc whole hlast).length = p.length + 1 := by simp [q]
  omega

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)

/-- **The content of Stacks Project, Tag 05UE.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a smooth morphism of finite
presentation whose fibres are geometrically irreducible of dimension `d`, and let `F` be an
`𝒪_X`-module of finite presentation which is flat over `S` in dimensions `≥ d`. Then `F` is
free of some finite rank on a neighbourhood of the generic point of every fibre. -/
theorem exists_freeAtPointOfRank_of_isFlatOverInDimensionsGE [Smooth f]
    (hf : FinitePresentation f)
    (hirr : ∀ s : S, GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s)) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : RelativeDimension f d) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    [F.IsFinitePresentation] (hflat : IsFlatOverInDimensionsGE f F d) (s : S) (ξ : f.fiber s)
    (hξ : IsGenericPoint ξ (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber s))) :
    ∃ r : ℕ, FreeAtPointOfRank F (f.fiberι s ξ) r := by
  have : IrreducibleSpace (f.fiber s) :=
    irreducibleSpace_fiber_of_geometricallyIrreducible f s (hirr s)
  -- `F` is flat over `S` at the generic point of the fibre through it.
  have hflatx : IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s ξ) := by
    by_contra hcon
    have hNsub : closure ({ξ} : Set (f.fiber s)) ⊆
        {y : f.fiber s | ¬ IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s y)} :=
      closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hcon)
        (isOpen_isFlatOverAt_fiber_of_locallyOfFiniteType f F s).isClosed_compl
    have hN : {y : f.fiber s | ¬ IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s y)}
        = Set.univ := by
      rw [show closure ({ξ} : Set (f.fiber s)) = Set.univ from hξ] at hNsub
      exact Set.eq_univ_of_univ_subset hNsub
    have hdimN : topologicalKrullDim
        ↥{y : f.fiber s | ¬ IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s y)} =
          topologicalKrullDim (f.fiber s) :=
      IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _
        ((Homeomorph.setCongr hN).trans (Homeomorph.Set.univ (f.fiber s))).isHomeomorph
    have hlt := (isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_iff_forall_topologicalKrullDim_lt f F d).mp hflat s
    rw [hdimN, (hd s ⟨ξ⟩).2] at hlt
    exact lt_irrefl _ hlt
  -- The restriction of `F` to the fibre has flat stalk at that generic point.
  obtain ⟨U, hU, n, ⟨e⟩⟩ :=
    Scheme.Modules.exists_iso_free_over_of_flat_over_at_of_flat_fiber_stalk f hf F
      (f.fiberι s ξ) hflatx
      (flat_fiber_stalk_isGenericPoint f _ (isGenericPoint_asFiber f s ξ hξ) (hirr _) F)
  exact ⟨n, freeAtPointOfRank_of_over_iso_free F hU n e⟩

/-- A module which is free of finite rank near a point of the source of a smooth morphism is
flat over the base at that point: it is finite locally free there and a smooth morphism is
flat. -/
theorem isFlatOverAt_of_freeAtPointOfRank [Smooth f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (x : X) (r : ℕ) (hfree : FreeAtPointOfRank F x r) :
    IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F x := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, hRank⟩ := hfree
  have h1 : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (F.restrict U.ι) r :=
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.of_iso.{u, u, u}
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback U.ι).app F).symm
      { exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRankData := hRank.exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRankData }
  have h2 : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (F.restrict U.ι) :=
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.isFiniteLocallyFree (F.restrict U.ι) r
  simpa using (isFlatOverAt_restrict_iff U.ι f F ⟨x, hxU⟩).mp
    (VectorBundleCodimensionOne.isFlatOver_of_isFiniteLocallyFree (U.ι ≫ f) (F.restrict U.ι)
      ⟨x, hxU⟩)

/-- The converse half of Stacks Project, Tag 05UE: if `F` is free of some finite rank near the
generic point of every fibre of a smooth morphism with geometrically irreducible fibres of
dimension `d`, then `F` is flat over the base in dimensions `≥ d`. -/
theorem isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_of_forall_exists_freeAtPointOfRank [Smooth f]
    (hirr : ∀ s : S, GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s)) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : RelativeDimension f d) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    [F.IsFinitePresentation]
    (h : ∀ (s : S) (ξ : f.fiber s), IsGenericPoint ξ (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber s)) →
      ∃ r : ℕ, FreeAtPointOfRank F (f.fiberι s ξ) r) :
    IsFlatOverInDimensionsGE f F d := by
  rw [isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_iff_forall_topologicalKrullDim_lt]
  intro s
  have : IrreducibleSpace (f.fiber s) :=
    irreducibleSpace_fiber_of_geometricallyIrreducible f s (hirr s)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := h s (genericPoint (f.fiber s)) (genericPoint_spec (f.fiber s))
  exact topologicalKrullDim_lt_of_isClosed_notMem
    (isOpen_isFlatOverAt_fiber_of_locallyOfFiniteType f F s).isClosed_compl
    (genericPoint (f.fiber s)) (by simpa using isFlatOverAt_of_freeAtPointOfRank f F _ r hr)
    (hd s ⟨genericPoint (f.fiber s)⟩).2

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 05UE.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a smooth morphism of affine schemes with
geometrically irreducible fibres of dimension `d` and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module
of finite presentation. Then `F` is flat over `S` in dimensions `≥ d` if and only if `F` is
free of some finite rank on a neighbourhood of the generic point of every fibre.

This is the decomposition `F_d = ∐_p H_p` of the source read on sections: `H_p` of Stacks 05MP
is freeness of the fixed rank `p` near every fibre's generic point, and the right hand side is
the union of the `H_p`. Since every hypothesis is stable under base change, the equivalence over
`S` carries the same equivalence over every scheme `T` over `S`. -/
@[stacks 05UE "F_d is the union of the H_p"]
theorem isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_iff_forall_exists_freeAtPointOfRank [IsAffine X] [IsAffine S]
    [Smooth f] (hirr : ∀ s : S, GeometricallyIrreducible (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s)) {d : ℕ}
    (hd : RelativeDimension f d) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    [F.IsFinitePresentation] :
    IsFlatOverInDimensionsGE f F d ↔
      ∀ (s : S) (ξ : f.fiber s), IsGenericPoint ξ (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber s)) →
        ∃ r : ℕ, FreeAtPointOfRank F (f.fiberι s ξ) r :=
  ⟨fun hflat ↦ exists_freeAtPointOfRank_of_isFlatOverInDimensionsGE f
      ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩ hirr hd F hflat,
    isFlatOverInDimensionsGE_of_forall_exists_freeAtPointOfRank f hirr hd F⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
